From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taiga-expanded <taiga-expanded@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:31:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ext: features on origin planes with an offset (datum planes)

A goal feature with "off" is sketched on the origin plane normal to (nx, ny, nz)
(Select:Plane:YZ / XZ / XY), shifted by off along that axis, and padded or
pocketed symmetrically: cross bores through the whole part (e.g. a piston-pin
or crank bore through a cylinder wall), through windows and cross pins/lugs.
No new commands: the model picks the plane, the runtime applies the offset
(AttachmentOffset, sign taken from the plane's own normal) and the symmetric
extrusion (Midplane, or SideType where available).
- ext/faces.py: is_datum, support_for -> Plane:*, apply_plane_offset,
  set_symmetric; goal encoding gains "off"
- session: two hooks (NewSketch offset, symmetric pad/pocket)
- ext/sampler.py: split "plane" (box or cylinder base, 1-2 datum features);
  training mixes side and plane goals
- evaluate: suite "plane" (level 3, seed offset 50000)
Tests: datum support, offset sign, symmetric setter, encoding, sampler geometry.
